# ============================================================================
# GitHub Token for Cloud Agent (write access to issues, PRs, labels, milestones)
# ============================================================================
# The gh CLI uses GH_TOKEN as its auth mechanism.
# Configure ONE of these in Cursor Dashboard > Cloud Agents > Secrets:
#
#   Option A (recommended): GH_TOKEN=ghp_your_personal_access_token
#     → Directly used by gh CLI, no mapping needed
#
#   Option B: PAGEKIT_BACKGROUND_AGENT=ghp_your_personal_access_token
#     → Mapped to GH_TOKEN in install.sh/start.sh
#
# Required scopes: repo (full control of private repositories)
# Generate at: https://github.com/settings/tokens
#
# ⚠️  PUBLIC REPOS: Cursor may NOT inject secrets into Cloud Agent VMs for
#     public repositories unless explicitly allowed. If secrets don't appear
#     as env vars, check Cursor docs for "secret injection for public repos".
#
# ⚠️  DUPLICATE WARNING: If you set BOTH GH_TOKEN and PAGEKIT_BACKGROUND_AGENT,
#     PAGEKIT_BACKGROUND_AGENT takes priority (see install.sh).
# ============================================================================
# GH_TOKEN=ghp_your_personal_access_token_here
# PAGEKIT_BACKGROUND_AGENT=ghp_your_personal_access_token_here

# Optional: Composer GitHub Token (if you hit rate limits)
# COMPOSER_GITHUB_TOKEN=your_github_token_here

# Optional: Database credentials for testing
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_NAME=pagekit_test
DB_USER=root
DB_PASSWORD=

# Optional: Email testing credentials
MAILER_DSN=smtp://localhost:1025
